# "Each opponent mills that many cards" (CR 615.5, 701.17a, 101.4): in a three-player game The Mindskinner (10/1, can't be
# blocked) attacks Bot2. The 10 combat damage it would deal to Bot2 is prevented, and both opponents mill 10 - Bot3 too, though
# it was dealt nothing - while Bot1, its controller, mills none. Libraries: Bot2 22 after its turn-2 draw, Bot3 22 after its
# turn-3 draw, each then 12; Bot1's 5 after its turn-1 draw (CR 103.8a: no skip in a multiplayer game) and turn-4 draw stays 5.
[Bot1 Deck]
The Mindskinner
Black Lotus
Island x12
[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30
[Bot3 Deck]
Island x30
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.The Mindskinner.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot2.Library.Count = 22
? Bot3.Library.Count = 22
Bot1.Attack(The Mindskinner > Bot2)
[T4 Bot1.Main2]
[Expect]
Prevented = 10 The Mindskinner > Bot2 by The Mindskinner
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot3.Life = 20
Bot2.Library.Count = 12
Bot3.Library.Count = 12
Bot1.Library.Count = 5
